    "independent_general_proof": "Let original lower-right corner be C=(6,0), crease endpoints Q=(q,0),R=(6,H), reflected corner A=(0,a), and d=6-q. Theta is the actual angle QRC. Thus d=L sin(theta),H=L cos(theta), so d/H=tan(theta). The crease preserves distances: AQ=CQ=d and AR=CR=H. AQ^2=q^2+a^2=d^2 gives a^2=12d-36. AR^2=36+(H-a)^2=H^2 gives2aH=36+a^2=12d, hence a=6d/H=6tan(theta). Therefore36tan^2(theta)=12d-36, so d=3sec^2(theta), L=3sec^2(theta)csc(theta), answer A. No measured renderer angle is used.",
    "hypotheses_considered": [
